# Mob consolidation: open questions on the Python C4 / yang.python track
Members that answered (read-only, independent): codex gpt-6.1-sol, claude fable-5-1, glm-5.3, deepseek-v4-pro. cmd qwen/qwen3.8-max produced only a one-line preamble twice (headless cmd -p withholds tools; counted as no answer). Answers: collab/1792200000000-mob-{codex,fable,glm,deepseek}.findings.md.

## Q1 I3 landing: UNANIMOUS B (drop the linked REPL path; land publication, DHT import, artifact, __all__, no-install assertions, the :admit seam)
All four: the two open findings live only in REPL wiring the fix round added; I3's acceptance (yang.antlr.md 3201-3204) has no REPL or foreign-principal element; foreign principals are a prerequisite (L-e), not a deliverable; A is a separate slice (per-[id revision] session/runtime state, F2 territory); C unacceptable.
Revert details (the one disagreement): codex drops `py/run-session` too and recomputes goldens; fable and glm KEEP `py/run-session` (the goldens were minted on it, the drop touches no prelude bytes, no re-mint). Orchestrator choice: keep `py/run-session` (two of three, no golden churn). Hunks to drop: frontends.cljc linked manifest/second install; antlr/repl.cljc linked-profile section (require-node, lower-linked-session, link-admission, linked-binding, publication require); yin/repl.cljc admit staging (three hunks, drive-links back to 2-arity); the linked-REPL tests incl. a-linked-import-only-another-principal-asserts-is-refused-test (park them for F2). Recorded gap text: fable's and glm's wording (no REPL frontend runs Python under the linked profile; :admit enforced only where a composition passes it; linked REPL profile = its own slice after F2 with a session keyed by [id revision] and admission at the module-exposure seam). Process: put I3's acceptance text and the gap record in the round-3 reviewer prompt.
## Q2 L-e and the interim
Agreement: L-e must verify closure origin and store ownership recursively (exports, re-exports, transitive dependency slices) before any executable value is exposed, with forged :store-of tests on all four VMs, plus ruling 19's remainder (authenticated publication, dependency pins, primitive/effect admission, store-context transitions). A link-time-only refusal is bypassable (cached/installed modules). Disagreement: deepseek says a refusal-only interim is not worth shipping (name check, not origin check); codex says do not build machinery just for an interim; fable and glm say keep the composition seam (cheap, exercised by the DHT tests) and enforce at install/exposure, not link time. Recommendation: keep the :admit seam (already in B), claim nothing at the REPL until L-e, never per-frontend admission.
## Q3 DHT blob cap
Agreement: acceptance honestly met for pym.m (JVM bytes consumed without republishing on Node/Dart); `py` is an installed pin until large blobs travel; record it. Do not raise the global cap to 1 MB and do not split py into smaller modules; A stays the only code identity. Disagreement on the fix: codex/deepseek/fable chunk below the linker (deepseek ties it to slice L-f, fable to the phase-8 cutover since images re-address); glm adds an immediate `:max-message-bytes` option on join as a composition knob plus real store-message chunking. Recommendation: chunked transport below the linker as a DHT-seat task; a join option is acceptable as a stopgap; decide the part format at the register-VM cutover.
## Q4 linker gap (dependency-binding is the only guard)
Agreement: real; linker seat owns it; the design doc's 7.4 sentence ("adds no rule the linker lacks") is false and must be corrected; fix = discharge step 5b compares the pinned manifest address with the installed dependency (transitive). Gating: codex says before I4 landing; fable says blocks L-d and so I4; glm says fold into L-d before I4; deepseek says does not block I4, must precede L-e. Recommendation: land it with/inside L-d, before I4.
## Q5 sequencing
Common: F2 first (it owns the dropped linked profile; REPL-only, no pinned addresses). Then Q4 fix + L-d, then I4. Wait for the register-VM cutover: C2 S5, safepoints 3-4 (all four), I7 (fable, glm). Disagreement on I5/I6: codex defers I5-I7 to after the cutover; deepseek and fable do I5/I6 before it; glm waits I5/I6/I7 (I5 re-mints addresses twice). Recommendation: F2, Q4+L-d, I4, then decide I5/I6 timing at the cutover plan.
## Q6 process
Common: stop on satisfied gates, not a round count; different-family review untouched; known-gaps ledger (gap | evidence | owner seat | closing slice | severity); reviewer prompts quote the slice row and acceptance; blocking = P0/P1 (or P2 in claimed acceptance) inside the slice's scope; fix rounds may not add public entry points, catalog ids or frontends; a finding in code the slice should not have written means REVERT, not fix; a disputed in-scope P1 goes to a third-family Architect, not a third engineer round. Recommendation: adopt as the standing rule (owner to confirm).

